// CALL FOLLOWER, the third thing Old School puts on this tab beside Equipment Stats and Items Kept
// on Death. NOT part of the 474 conversion above - 474 had only the two, because followers came
// later - so a rerun of tools/models/port474if.py will drop these two records and they have to go
// back.
//
// THE ICON AND THE PLACE ARE OLD SCHOOL'S OWN. Its interface 387 puts four buttons along the bottom
// at x=7, 52, 97 and 142, and Call follower is the last of them, drawn from sprite group 1343 - the
// whistle, in sprites/osrs_call_follower.png. This tab has two of the four (474 had no guide prices
// either), at x=45 and x=113, so the whistle goes to the right of them where its own order puts it.
// ...and the same frame the other two sit in, which it did not have: sixteen 9x9 pieces, the
// offsets copied from the two frames above. Without it the whistle was a bare icon floating to the
// right of two framed buttons.
